            {
              "label": "Discontinuity",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-plot-discontinuity"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Reject non-finite values and inspect asymptotes. FunctionGraph2D filters invalid/extreme samples; connecting the remaining finite points can still join across a discontinuity. Split the domain into separate plots where the mathematical function is disconnected. Reuse typed arrays when sample count is stable and avoid dense resampling for every pointer event."
        }
      ]
